[
    {
        "id": "sdb-note",
        "type": "comment",
        "z": "synth-bench-tab",
        "name": "synthetic-defects feeds golden-compare the frames it made, with the answers",
        "info": "`synthetic-defects` draws a label, paints a known defect into it,\nphotographs the result through a camera model, and sends one message\nper frame. Each frame carries the golden it was made from\n(`msg.golden`, plus `msg.goldenKey` so `golden-compare` prepares that\ngolden once for the whole run) and the exact ground truth\n(`msg.synth`).\n\nSo `golden-compare` here needs no golden path and no configuration at\nall: it takes the reference off the message. Read the two debug nodes\nside by side - `msg.result` is what the node decided,\n`msg.synth.expected` is what the frame actually contained. A frame\nwhose `expected.pass` is false and whose `result.pass` is true is a\nmiss; the reverse is a false alarm on a part that was supposed to\npass. Wire an image-preview node onto `msg.payload` to see the defect\nthat produced it.\n\nDefaults are 87 frames at 500ms apart, roughly a second each to\ngenerate at 1500x2100 - inject once and watch. Narrow it with the\nfamily and severity checkboxes, or send `msg.families` /\n`msg.severities`. A new inject stops the run in progress.\n\nThis is a test bench, not a production flow. For scored numbers -\nrecall per family and severity, false-fail rate, sweeps - use\n`bench/synth/generate.js` and `bench/synth/run.js` offline.",
        "x": 400,
        "y": 60,
        "wires": []
    },
